WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome back, everybody.
We have a little --

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.701
We have a special guest
with us right now.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:04.968
-Yes.
This is Diamond Baby.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:08.033
-Hi, Diamond Baby.
Nice to see you.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.267
I thought that would be
the biggest surprise,

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.033
but we also have
another surprise.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.100
Your mom is here.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.934
Ladies and gentlemen,
Kathy Hilton.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.868
♪♪

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.367
-Yes!

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.400
You are unbelievable.
-Mwah!

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.968
-You are the funniest person
on television right now.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.601
-Hi, Mom.
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.601
-Hi, honey. How are you?
-You look beautiful.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.067
-Mwah!
-Now, I thought it'd be fun

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.267
to have both
of you guys together

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:34.434
and play a game with you.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.100
Because you always give out
great advice.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.334
And I thought, right now,
it would be fun.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:38.400
We could help some people out

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.901
with their big-time
life decisions.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.767
It's time for "Life Coach
with Paris and Kathy Hilton."

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:48.968
-♪ Life Coach
with Paris and Kathy ♪

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.534
-So, we had viewers
send in some questions.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.567
We've got some pretty good ones.
How about this one?

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.467
-Well, I know those people.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.033
I would just say,
show the picture once.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.000
'Cause nobody really cares,
truthfully.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:13.000
-That's so mean.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.167
-One picture.
That's enough.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:15.167
-They don't really --
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.200
That's true.
-They don't care.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.701
-But when you first
become a parent, though,

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.634
all you do is show pictures
to everybody.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.234
I'm showing my cab driver.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.567
I'm like,
"Dude, look at my baby.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.834
And he's like, "Yeah."
-That was Rick, my husband.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:28.968
-Okay. He showed it
to everybody, yeah.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.801
-I think that's so rude because
you could really hurt someone,

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.534
and people are really struggling
right now.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.567
And it's just not nice.
If you don't have something

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.801
nice to say,
don't say anything at all.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:51.834
-I love that.
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.767
Can't top that.
I agree with you.

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.601
Don't do that.
-No, that's mean.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:57.601
I love that.
All right. How about this?

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:08.801
-I wasted three years
on my cellphone and my iPad.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.167
No, I'm not kidding.
-Three years of your life gone.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:14.767
-Three years gone.
Wasting, just sitting there.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.501
And it would get dark.
-Wow.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:19.000
And what do you do now?
-Now I'm working.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.601
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, so, you don't need --

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:21.934
How about you?

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.734
-I would probably need
to ask that advice, as well,

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.400
because I'm addicted
to my phone.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.734
-That question came from you.
All right, perfect.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:31.534
-It was me.
-I heard, like,

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.601
if you want to -- when you go
to bed, you put the phone --

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.434
you charge it in another room.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.400
No?
-I need the alarm.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.734
I need a sleep fan
or something.

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.934
I don't know. I can't sleep
without, like, a noise.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.067
-You too, right?
-We both have the fans.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:45.734
-[ Laughs ]
Oh, my --

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.734
All right.
How about this?

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.901
-Wear sunglasses.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:01.868
-Wow! A pro!
-I love it.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.300
-Wow, a pro right there.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.200
Don't stop rolling.
Just wear sunglasses.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.400
Perfect.
Probably goes with your ape.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.300
-I can relate to that,
but it's the opposite.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.033
I'm the night owl,
and then, my husband is, like,

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.033
the early riser
and goes to bed early.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:30.567
So, I try to get him
to stay up later.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:33.067
So, I don't know.
Just try to change

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:35.701
your sleeping schedule
or tell the other person

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:38.367
to wake up earlier or something.
-The other person.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.801
-Wow.
Kathy, any advice on that?

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.767
-I would -- I think I'm --
Rick goes to bed.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.501
I stay up later on the iPad.
So, I think he's got to

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.167
get an iPad
so we can do it together.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.767
-You're both on the iPad?
Yeah.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.767
All right, this one says...

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.100
-I know who wrote this question.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.434
-You do?
-I do.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:05.634
Don't you know?
-No.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:06.968
-I think I do.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:09.400
I think it's the octopus,
Carter.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.501
-What?
-What?

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:14.634
-We call Carter the Groomzilla
and the Octopus.

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.701
-'Cause he's got his mitts
into everything.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.634
-So, you think Carter
wrote this.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.467
-Read it again.
-"I want to quit my job

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.901
and travel, but I'm afraid of
finding work when I'm back.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.534
Should I just do it anyway?"
-What?

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.167
It has nothing to do with him.
-Well, because --

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:30.200
-He did travel with you on
a long holiday, your honeymoon.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.968
-Yeah, but he's working
non-stop.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.968
-I know.
-With this new world,

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.667
you can work from anywhere
with Zoom.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:36.934
-I get it.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.334
-Wow, wow.
The Octopus.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:40.567
Oh, my God.
-No, he does.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:41.801
He's got his mitts
into everything.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.033
And Paris is right.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.234
She goes,
"Mommy, he means well."

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:48.167
But he was offending me.
He was calling the cake place.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.400
He was calling the band.
He was calling --

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.701
-Talking about the wedding?
-The party planner.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.467
-Yes, he's very organized.
-The band, the hotels.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:55.601
Everything.
-But he's the groom.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.934
-I know.
I said, "This is not normal."

00:04:57.934 --> 00:04:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.234
He even picked out
the invitation

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:04.400
and the save-the-date cards.
I was like, "Okay."

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.734
-He's just very responsible,
very organized, and we're not.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.300
-What do you guys think?
Come on?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.334
[ Laughter ]
-All, right, how about this?

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.334
Ready?

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:24.267
-To me, I really think that you
send out love and good wishes.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.901
And I just put, like --

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:30.167
If they're unkind,
put, like, a little sad emoji.

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:32.434
[ Laughter ]
No, I mean that, really.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:33.868
-Just let them know it's sad.
-The fact that

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:37.300
they're giving you attention,
they do care about you.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.434
So, then I just write,
"Oh, I'm sorry

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:42.634
if I offended you,"
or I put an emoji like that.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.567
And then, they're sweet,
and they feel bad.

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:45.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.534
-Kill them with kindness.
I like that.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.167
-Yes.
Grandma used to say that.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:50.467
-All right, good.
Kill them with kindness.

00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:51.567
I'll take that.
I love it.

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.067
That is all the time we have for

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:55.801
"Life Coach
with Paris and Kathy Hilton."

